# AI Coding Rules

> For Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and Gemini Code Assist on this repo.

This project is an autonomous research assistant: FastAPI backend, React 18 + Vite frontend, LangChain orchestration, Claude tool_use calls, Qdrant storage, and async search against arXiv and Semantic Scholar.

## Core Rules

- Prefer small, local changes over broad refactors.
- Keep type hints on new or modified Python code; preserve mypy-friendly signatures.
- Use async-first I/O everywhere: `httpx.AsyncClient` for HTTP, `async def` for endpoints and services, and `asyncio.to_thread()` for CPU-bound work.
- Never add `requests` to async code paths.
- Wrap external API calls with retry logic, using `tenacity` with exponential backoff.
- Read required configuration from environment variables or config objects; do not hard-code secrets or operational limits.
- Keep token limits, paper counts, timeouts, and batch sizes configurable unless the code already establishes a safe constant.
- Cache repeated work when the same paper or session input can produce the same result.

## Backend Rules

- FastAPI endpoints should define `response_model` and `status_code`.
- Keep background agent work explicit and await it in the request lifecycle unless the code already uses a dedicated task runner.
- Add request ID tracing middleware when touching API entry points.
- Validate all user input with Pydantic models before it reaches search, ranking, embedding, or Claude calls.
- Keep agent tools single-purpose. Search, ranking, clustering, extraction, and synthesis should remain separate functions.
- Truncate paper text before Claude calls and before embedding when the code path expects summaries or abstracts only.
- Use structured JSON outputs for model-driven extraction instead of free-form text whenever the result will be consumed by code.
- Keep Qdrant operations explicit: collection config, bounded searches, and payloads on upsert.

## Frontend Rules

- Use React functional components only.
- Use Zustand for shared agent state; do not introduce Redux or React Context for cross-component session state.
- Keep the wide-screen layout pattern already established in the repo.
- Use Tailwind utility classes instead of inline styles.
- Render a loading skeleton while the agent is running.
- Wrap output rendering in an error boundary so a bad markdown render does not crash the app.
- Use `EventSource` for streaming progress updates and close the stream on complete or error.

## Testing Rules

- Add or update tests when behavior changes.
- Mock HTTP calls and Claude responses in unit tests.
- Keep tests async where the code under test is async.
- Do not introduce live API calls in CI.
- Favor targeted tests for the touched module or behavior instead of broad snapshots.

## Assistant-Specific Guidance

- Cursor: inspect nearby code before editing, and avoid multi-file refactors unless the change truly requires them.
- GitHub Copilot: accept async completions only after checking they do not introduce blocking calls or new sync HTTP.
- Gemini Code Assist: when explaining a change, note any Claude token-budget impact if the change affects prompts, batching, or output size.

## Practical Constraints

- Do not log secrets, raw paper content, or user research topics at info level.
- Preserve per-session isolation for embeddings and review state.
- Prefer `asyncio.gather()` for independent concurrent calls such as arXiv and Semantic Scholar search.
- Keep prompt templates and model settings consistent with the repo unless the user explicitly asks for a change.
